        "number": 8,
        "internalPageId": null,
        "title": "1 Verbs using infinitives I want to say I’m sorry. They decided to keep on that. Check a list here: https://www.engvid.com/english-resource/verbs-followed-by-gerunds-and-infinitives/ 2 Verbs using gerunds He kept eating junk food. Stop bothering your sister! 3 Verbs using both I started to work here last June. I started working here last June. 4 Infinitive after adjectives It is important to come clean. It is awful to spill the beans. There is another way to use gerunds 5 Gerunds after prepositions I thought about telling her. Make him happy by bringing cookies. -",
        "visibleTexts": [
          "1 Verbs using infinitives I want to say I’m sorry. They decided to keep on that. Check a list here: https://www.engvid.com/english-resource/verbs-followed-by-gerunds-and-infinitives/ 2 Verbs using gerunds He kept eating junk food. Stop bothering your sister! 3 Verbs using both I started to work here last June. I started working here last June. 4 Infinitive after adjectives It is important to come clean. It is awful to spill the beans. There is another way to use gerunds 5 Gerunds after prepositions I thought about telling her. Make him happy by bringing cookies. -",
          "https://www.engvid.com/english-resource/verbs-followed-by-gerunds-and-infinitives/",
          "There are many ways in which we can state our ideas, opinions and apologies. Using infinitives and gerunds is one of them."
